title: 'eth-rpc: bump subxt to 0.51 so signed v4 extrinsics can be decoded'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The workspace `subxt`, `subxt-metadata`, `subxt-rpcs` and `subxt-signer` dependencies move from
    0.50 to 0.51. subxt 0.50 could not decode signed v4 extrinsics on runtimes that declare more
    than one transaction extension version, such as Polkadot Asset Hub runtime 2005000.

    In `pallet-revive-eth-rpc`, `frame-benchmarking-cli`, `pallet-revive` (`std` feature) and the
    `subxt_client` module of `sc-statement-store` (`test-helpers` feature), public items that use
    subxt or subxt-signer types now use their 0.51 versions. Code that passes subxt or subxt-signer
    values to these items should use version 0.51 of both crates; the subxt changelog lists the
    breaking changes.

    `pallet_revive_eth_rpc::client::ClientError` no longer has a `Jsonrpsee` variant. `connect` now
    reports a failure to build the node RPC client as `ClientError::RpcError`, so code that matched
    `ClientError::Jsonrpsee` should match `ClientError::RpcError` instead.

    eth-rpc deployments need no configuration change.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: major
- name: frame-benchmarking-cli
  bump: major
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: minor
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: minor
